<title>USA: Japan Airlines, Air France in code-share agreement.</title>
<headline>Japan Airlines, Air France in code-share agreement.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan Airlines Co Ltd on Thursday said it reached a new code-share agreement with Air France for flights between Tokyo and Istanbul via Paris.</p>
<p>The Japanese carrier will begin operating the daily flights on April 1, pending government approval, the company said.</p>
<p>Japan Airlines said it was the first Japanese airline to offer flights to Turkey. Air France now operates a Paris-to-Istanbul flight independently, it said.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
